SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
Subject: [PATCH] Use defined unaligned accesses in the private sanitizer VM

Keep alignment checking enabled. These changes are only for the private
test kernel, never for the host or the standalone module package.

Use unaligned access helpers for firmware data, instruction operands,
string destinations and inflate copies. Select ACPICA's portable byte
accesses. Traverse ordinary and RCU list sentinels through their actual
node alignment, and use the underlying SMP structure alignment for queues
shared with IRQ and wakeup nodes; retain the aligned CSD allocation typedef.
Select naturally aligned widths for no-fault copy operands on all architectures.

